Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:43:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] MT-FIX1: review fixes (C++) -- window registry no
 longer stuck "open" after an HMI refresh, registry accepted during alarm
 dialogs, Motor Power carries its direction, post-Poll loop step gated, jog
 re-sends the bar's values

From the adversarial review of 2c1afab / eef1a78 / 5a0f02d (20260925-26), C++ side (web side is web a5454b9):
- WebWindowRegistry: a stale connection's "open" was never forgotten and beat a fresh connection's "closed", so
  after an HMI refresh / WS reconnect with Motor Test or Teach open, fMotorTest read open forever -- and since
  MT-E3b golden MainProc pauses while those are open, production would stay paused. Now a form that has ANY fresh
  report is decided by the fresh reports only (union among them unchanged); only when every report is stale does
  contract section 6 (stale = open) apply, unchanged. New test [5b] + WebWindowRegistryAgeConnForTest().
- wb_serve modal wait answers ui.windows.put (inert, token-exempt, same reason as cfg.resync): a blocking alarm
  left unanswered past 15 s used to make every form stale = open.
- motorPowerToggle: refuses "relay-changed" when the live relay != the page's expectRelayOn, and a request with
  confirmOff=true (the operator answered "Sure to turn off motor power?") never powers ON.
- MotorAccessPollTick(be, operatorConnected): the step after every 1203 Poll is gated like the beat (operator gone
  -> CancelAllJobs; last beat's safe lock -> CancelAllJobs) BEFORE any leg is issued; wb_serve passes the live
  ControlOwner()!=0.
- Jog = golden: the jog re-sends the exact jog-family values the scroll bar (or the 1% selection) wrote
  (g_jogSpd), not MotorSpeedFromPct of today's MOT[] parameters (a cell edit / Copy From / Reload no longer
  changes the jog speed); a failed scroll-bar write keeps the slower of old/new.
- runtime / ack "cur" publish "selectable" (golden lM00Click :740-743 per build) so the SIM build can select.
Tests: WebMotorAccess 377/0 (new [14]), WebWindowRegistry, MotorPoints_HT9050, SjsonChan pass; production_audit 0 changes.
Not yet run on the machine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
